[Music]  there is nothing more american than  apple pie it is one of the most popular  and recognizable desserts in the world  hi my name is jordan i'm a producer here  at tasty and today we're going to do  something a little different recently  while thumbing through our new cookbook  i found this strange recipe for  something called a mock apple pie it  contains no apples and uses simple  crackers as a substitute which begs the  question how can something without  apples taste like apple pie so today i'm  going to make this recipe and feed it to  a few of my co-workers see if they can  spot the difference  [Music]  i'm going to start by sifting two cups  of flour with two teaspoons of sugar and  one teaspoon of salt then i'm going to  add 10 tablespoons of butter that have  cubes and chills i chilled the butter  beforehand because it's really important  to keep this cold the heat from my hands  should be enough to allow me to work the  butter into the flour i'm really just  kind of pressing my fingers working it  together until it forms a nice sandy  texture  i'm gonna add a third of a cup of cold  water as the water hydrates the flour  it'll develop a loose lumpy texture  that'll start to clump together on the  fork at this point i'll turn the dough  out and start to bring it together with  my hands  once it does come together into a nice  mound i'm going to cut it in half and  form each of the halves into nice round  half inch disks and i'm going to wrap  those in cling film and put them in the  fridge for an hour  while these pie crusts chill in the  fridge i'm going to move on to the  filling to start we're going to make a  simple syrup solution out of one and  three quarters cups of sugar with two  teaspoons of cream of tartar added to it  to that we're going to pour over one and  one-half cups of water once this mixture  has come to a boil and the sugar is  fully dissolved i'm going to reduce the  heat to low and let it simmer for about  15 minutes before taking it off the heat  now i'm going to add the only other  flavorings to the syrup  a half a teaspoon of cinnamon and the  zest and juice of one lemon  i know you can't smell this right now  but this combination of lemon juice  sugar and cinnamon smells exactly like  apple pie if the pie tastes like this  mixture smells we are going to trick a  lot of people so while that's happening  i'm going to preheat my oven and begin  to roll out my dough it's important to  rotate your dough as you roll it out  this will help you get a nice round  shape that will encompass the diameter  of whatever you're baking it in we're  going for a standard nine inch pie dish  so i want my dough to be at least an  inch or two larger than that on all  sides i'm going to use the rolling pin  to pick it back up and lay it over the  top next i'm going to gently use my  hands to press the dough into the bottom  of the pie dish  now we're on to the fun part the recipe  calls for 2 cups or about 4 ounces of  coarsely broken buttery crackers now in  order to make this work and deceive my  co-workers i think i need to keep these  in pretty large pieces if they're too  fine i'm afraid the syrup will turn them  into a thick paste that won't look  anything like an apple pie on the inside  once i've broken up all the crackers and  added them to the pie crust i'm going to  dot the top with another two tablespoons  of cubed butter as you would any normal  apple pie once i have my top crust on  i'm going to take that little bit of  overhang and tuck it under itself while  pressing it against the lip of the pie  dish next i'll use a fork to crimp the  edge of the dough all the way around  as a finishing touch before putting the  pie in the oven i'm going to give it a  light egg wash by beating one egg with  one tablespoon of water and brushing it  across the surface  and finally to make sure the pie doesn't  explode in the oven i'm going to cut a  small vent in the center to let the  steam escape  after 35 minutes i was left with this  from here i can tell you it smells like  an apple pie it looks like an apple pie  i am really excited to see what my  co-workers think when they have a slice  of this  okay so  loving this crust loving the you know  clean cut visually  it's on the mark and this looks fresh  and definitely homemade um you can see  the layers of apple they're like thinly  sliced which is great can i smell it  first  very suspicious  [Music]  i like it  i like that it's not as like there  aren't like obvious chunks of apple in  it because that always grosses me out  okay yeah it's sweet like you want it  the apples are like um perfectly  mushy cheers  you know i like this there's like  definitely you can taste the cinnamon  and the i don't know but  there's like other elements of it that  i'm not used to in apple pie it's good  the flavors are there but i would guess  like you use applesauce or something  like some kind of a  different apple would be my guest hold  on let me  what  oh my no wonder i actually like this one  oh my goodness now i can kind of see  that that's crazy  because the flavor is there so there's  no apples in this  so wait hold on okay  okay hold on so there's no apples but it  tastes a little bit like apples  these are crackers  i'm sorry so we're not eating we're not  eating apple pie i actually like this  way better than normal apple pie but the  one thing that now i realize is you can  see the little like ridges of the  crackers  i have a really good childhood friend  who's allergic to apples and can eat any  apple stuff i would like get this  cookbook to give to her and be like  here's your taste  of america  i think it compares to apple pie like  it's a pretty good replica and i'm not  gonna lie the worst part about preparing  a fruit pie like apple pie is when you  have to get like your mandolin or your  like slicer and start like peeling these  apples and coring them and chopping them  up so this is like a much easier way to  pull off an apple pie i feel like i  should be like oh weird but like i want  to keep eating it i mean it looked like  a pie smelled like pie tastes like a pie  i'm here for it i've been bamboozled but  i'm gonna eat it  how dare you  i will go on record and say that i  thought this was apples  but  if it's good it's good and if it's  delicious it's delicious and it was so  i i don't mind being being deceived i'm  done for this pie i'm i'm for it i'm  team mac if this is what the mock apple  pie tastes like i can't wait to try the  actual apple pie in the cookbook and so  now i'm super curious  this mock apple pie was a huge hit and a  really fun experiment nearly everyone  was fooled  if you want to try this recipe for  yourself make sure to check out our  newest cookbook tasty ultimate it  features dozens of never before seen  recipes tips tricks and recipe showdown  just like this one get your copy today  by clicking the link below  [Music]  you

